{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nOn 2026-11-13 the operator confirmed that rebar has no rule saying an agentic plan review that read no code is never signed. Change 3392 (`bf7d496eedc`, bug `bridal-gifted-vampirebat`) added that rule anyway. It came from an agent's reading of the epic's \"Fail closed\" invariant. That invariant covers runs that do not finish cleanly with schema-valid output. It says nothing about which tools the agent calls.\n\nToday an agentic run that completes cleanly but makes no `read_file`, `search_files` or `list_directory` call resolves to an unsigned INDETERMINATE (`resolution_class` FIX_AGENT_DESIGN) instead of the verdict its findings produce.\n\nWhere the rule lives on origin/main:\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`, around line 249: the `agentic_unread_error` check and its early return through `_degraded_plan_review_verdict`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`:\n  - `agentic_unread_error`, `_CODE_READ_TOOLS`;\n  - `STEP_AGENTIC_REVIEW` added to the required step ids, which exists only to keep that check from being silently disabled.\n- `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md` §3, around line 92: the \"An agentic run that read no code ... is never signed (amended 2026-11-13 ...)\" paragraph.\n- Tests:\n  - `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`, the section \"an agent that read no code is never signed\";\n  - `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py`, the real-runner `_usage` code-read tests.\n\n## Plan\n\nRemove exactly what `bf7d496eedc` added, so behavior returns to what it was before that commit:\n1. In `gate_dispatch.py`, remove the check and its early return.\n2. In `plan_review_recovery.py`, remove `agentic_unread_error` and `_CODE_READ_TOOLS`. Restore the required step-id set to its pre-`bf7d496eedc` contents. Remove `STEP_AGENTIC_REVIEW` unless something other than the rule uses it.\n3. In ADR 0123 §3, remove the paragraph. Add a dated 2026-11-13 amendment note saying it was withdrawn because the operator never decided it. Keep the existing \"Fail closed\" rule for failed runs unchanged.\n4. Remove the rule's tests. Add a RED test showing that an agentic run which completes cleanly with zero `blocker` findings and no code-read calls PASSes and is signed.\n5. Check the agentic success path is otherwise identical to its state at `aa1681bb531^` minus `bf7d496eedc`. A `git revert` of `bf7d496eedc`, resolved against the later ADR edits, is acceptable.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag. No other behavior change. The other fail-closed paths stay intact: errors, timeouts, limits, refusals and invalid output.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] `git grep -n -iE 'agentic_unread|read no code|_CODE_READ_TOOLS' -- src docs tests` prints nothing.\n- [x] A test shows a clean agentic run with zero blocker findings and no code-read calls PASSes and is signed.\n- [x] The existing fail-closed tests for failed agentic runs still pass, unchanged.\n- [x] ADR 0123 carries a dated 2026-11-13 note withdrawing the rule.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794608160538282764,"uuid":"c13f4254-a8d8-4f83-95bb-1b585eabdd32"}